<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Draw Polyline Nodes as Points</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from the</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>tree context menu for polylines &gt; Draw Polyline Nodes as &gt; Points</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span></b> <span class="Command">Draw Polyline Nodes as Points</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is available for polylines only. When you select it, all nodes of every polyline will be visualised as small yellow points.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command affects to all polyline groups in the active window although it was applied to a single polyline or polyline group. The other open windows are not influenced on it. The state of Draw Polyline Nodes as Points is not stored, i.e. next time when you open the file nodes will not be displayed.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP235990708" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><img src="../view_menu/Commands_files/image028.gif" width="328px" height="216px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="Warning" id="P1"><span lang="EN-GB">Points are not displayed if you select</span> <span class="Mode">Points</span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span class="Mode">Large Points</span><span lang="EN-GB">, or</span> <span class="Mode">Polygons</span> <span lang="EN-GB">render mode from the viewport context menu.</span></p>
